    "body": "I think the current PR still makes sense.\r\n\r\nIn addition I would suggest that we remove\r\n\r\n> If [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this) is in the [popover showing state](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#popover-showing-state), then throw an [\"InvalidStateError\"](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#invalidstateerror) [DOMException](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-DOMException).\r\n\r\nfrom `dialog`'s `show()` as it's not fundamentally incompatible with also being a popover. As we demonstrate in this PR the salient piece of information is really top layer participation and `show()` doesn't do that so it should not introduce unnecessary coupling.",
